<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cuntz et al. (2010) PLoS Comput. Biol. & Cuntz et al. (2007) PNAS Ramón y Cajal minimum-wiring and conduction-delay greedy Steiner dendritic trees + Rall's 3/2 diameter power law — MorphoEval overall 52.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 (v1) baseline evaluation of `2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py` (weighted score: 54.1/100). The Pass 1 baseline implements only a minimal 2-point comparison at bf=0.0 and bf=0.8 on N=80 circular points without sweeping the full Cuntz et al. (2010) Pareto trade-off curve across bf in [0, 1], omits Rall's (1959) 3/2 electrotonic diameter power law tapering (d_p^(3/2) = d_1^(3/2) + d_2^(3/2)), omits the Wen-Chklovskii / Cuntz 2D (W propto N^(1/2) A^(1/2)) and 3D (W propto N^(2/3) V^(1/3)) wiring scaling laws, omits a random non-optimal spanning tree negative control, and does not segment or analyze the vendored Santiago Ramón y Cajal (1899) Purkinje dendritic arbor specimen (`cajal_purkinje_dendritic_arbor_specimen.jpg`). Overall 52.8/100 (faithfulness 50.0, reproducibility 59.2); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 56, Morphological realism / specimen match 44, Parameter expressivity 50, Morphometric validation 52, Source and data traceability 68, Code-to-model traceability 56, Reproducibility package 54. Output judged: docs/media/cajal_dendritic_wiring_comparison.png: rendered output of 2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py at 8871db0, image/png, 118924 B, 1300×624 px, artifact_sha256 db0abb4568b420716b846ebaec024a48f2247147781aa037c4bdae1fbe246710 (sha256 db0abb4568b420716b846ebaec024a48f2247147781aa037c4bdae1fbe246710), spec_fingerprint e3fe84c50afe7ec7f86e9cbcdd65b055eae449029956d538ecfdcce95c4d6fa6. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: e3fe84c50afe7ec7f86e9cbcdd65b055eae449029956d538ecfdcce95c4d6fa6; artifact_sha256: db0abb4568b420716b846ebaec024a48f2247147781aa037c4bdae1fbe246710; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/cajal_dendritic_wiring_reference.json=8f1cb50f696dbce1..., datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/cajal_purkinje_dendritic_arbor_specimen.jpg=6255a396655b56c4..., datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/paper_citations.bib=6925a1fc3e146cab..., datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/scout_manifest.json=2440e61b14fedf53...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Implement the full Cuntz et al. (2010) TREES-toolbox greedy MST algorithm across balancing factor bf in [0, 1], reproducing cerebellar Purkinje / Drosophila Class IV da (bf=0.20), cortical pyramidal / Class III (bf=0.40), and motoneuron / Class I (bf=0.70) arbors alongside a random non-optimal spanning tree negative control.",
        "remediation needed: Segment and skeletonize Santiago Ramón y Cajal's (1899) human cerebellar Purkinje neuron specimen (`cajal_purkinje_dendritic_arbor_specimen.jpg`) to extract the empirical Sholl intersection profile, skeletonized branch-point count, and box-counting fractal dimension (D_f = 1.7817), backed by runtime SHA-256 integrity checks and an 8-suite `--self-test`.",
        "remediation needed: Verify the Wen & Chklovskii (2008) / Cuntz et al. (2010) 2D planar (W propto N^(1/2) A^(1/2)) and 3D volumetric (W propto N^(2/3) V^(1/3)) wiring scaling laws across N in [25, 320] and implement Rall's (1959) 3/2 electrotonic diameter tapering law d_parent^(3/2) = sum_k d_daughter_k^(3/2)." ;
    pk:hasScore 5.28e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

